# Environment for the SHARED Resilient Autonomy Lab instance — one container
# serving every visitor.
#
# THIS APP READS NOTHING FROM HERE. It is Caddy serving a directory of static
# files: the project's rendered documents, its measured-run evidence, and an
# operator console replaying frames exported from a real rosbag. There is no
# database, no account, no per-visitor state and no outbound call, which is
# also why `mode: "shared"` is correct rather than merely cheap — two visitors
# cannot see each other's anything, because there is nothing to see.
#
# Copy this file to breakmyrobot.shared.env on the VPS anyway. The broker
# starts the app without it (it logs `no env file at …` and carries on), but
# `gateway/deploy.sh` reports MISSING for every manifest service that has no
# env file, and a permanent MISSING is noise that hides a real one.
#
#   cp breakmyrobot.shared.env.example breakmyrobot.shared.env
#   chown root:1000 breakmyrobot.shared.env && chmod 640 breakmyrobot.shared.env
#
# No GATEWAY_SECRET: that exists so an app can tell the broker's identity
# headers from a client's. This app serves the same bytes to everyone and
# reads no header, so a secret here would be a value with nothing to protect.

TZ=UTC
